q-cyborg-soldier and cs-cyborg-strike-trooper; the book files the Republic''s cyborgs with no group heading. The soldier states no pool, so the line picks its S.D.C. roll; a dragon ''borg states mdc_base, and the line is kept so the five agree. || BODY: the class covers partial and full conversion, so the class itself states NO mdc_base, as fq-cyborg-soldier and cs-cyborg-strike-trooper do; a partial conversion is a living human with bionic limbs. The four body types of printed 96 are variants: the two FULL bodies carry the typical (first) figures as fixed attribute_dice (P.S., P.P., Spd) and their printed M.D.C. without additional armor as mdc_base (110 and 180); the two PARTIAL bodies override nothing, because their P.S./P.P./Spd are the bionic limbs'' and not the character''s. The maximum figures, touch percentages, Prowl penalties, sizes and weights are prose in the Bionic Body ability; the Prowl penalties are conditional on body and armor, so they are not subtracted from any skill. The four dragon ''borgs (printed 101-108) are their own classes. || SKILLS: catalog base plus printed bonus: Mathematics: Basic 45+10, Radio: Basic 45+10, Computer Operation 40+10, Jet Packs 42+20 (printed Pilot Jet Pack), Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+10, Find Contraband 26+10 (printed Find Contraband, Weapons & Cybernetics), Land Navigation 36+10, Climbing 40+10, Swimming 50+10. Literacy: Japanese at 98% stored as Literacy: Native Language at the book''s 98, fixed; Language: Japanese 98% as Language: Native Tongue; one language of choice (+15%) as a Language: Other pick. W.P. Heavy Energy Weapons is W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons, as fq-cyborg-soldier stores it. Hand to Hand: Basic Martial Arts/Judo is this book''s row; the upgrade prices (Aikido or Karate one pick, Jujitsu two) are the hand_to_hand block. The Jet Packs figure is the soldier''s +20% in all five; a body''s own bonus to jet pack piloting stays in that body''s prose. || RELATED: five plus one at levels 4, 8 and 12. SECONDARY: none at level one; two each at levels 2, 5, 8 and 13, as printed (the FQ soldier''s ninth-level slot is 8 here), from the related list excluding those marked None and without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the standard military issue (printed 98), identical in all five Republic cyborg classes: the energy rifle is unspecified, so it is a choice of this book''s ArmaTech and H-Brand energy rifles (the stun rifle and the underwater rifle left out); four extra E-clips are the rifle E-clip row; four grenades are a choice of this book''s grenades excluding the armor dissolver, as printed (four of one kind; a mix is the GM''s call); distancing binoculars are infrared-distancing-binoculars; the backpack is pr-1-standard-backpack, this book''s standard pack. The body-styling ammunition, maintenance and repairs are not items, and the jet pack, hover vehicle and extra weapons available upon assignment are not starting kit. The Cyborg Body Armor plates (printed 97) have no catalog rows and are not stubbed: they are prose in an ability. || MONEY: monthly salary 2,000 credits (officers of 9th level and up 3,500 to 5,000; police ''borgs 800 more than an unaugmented officer); starting_money holds the 1D6x1000 the book gives as a first-level character''s savings. Room, board, clothing and medical care are provided. The text layer ciphers the savings as !D6xlOOO."
